    "created_at": "2025-01-02T20:51:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-02T20:52:32Z",
    "body": "Because `./` path components are ignored in [URL path parsing](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#path-state), so the pathname is simply the result of resolving `foo/bar` relative to the `/` implied in the base URL, which is `/foo/bar`.\r\n\r\n```js\r\nnew URL('./foo/bar', 'https://example.com').toString()\r\n// 'https://example.com/foo/bar'\r\n```\r\n\r\nUnless I'm misunderstanding your question?",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
