    "updated_at": "2025-01-03T20:10:37Z",
    "body": "I think the issue may be in step 17 of __process a URLPatternInit__, where the spec says \"_baseURL_ has an opaque path\" but I suspect should read \"_baseURL_ does not have an opaque path\".\r\n\r\nChromium's implementation is `baseURL.IsHierarchical()` (which corresponds to this concept, modulo a feature change) and this check appears missing altogether from urlpattern-polyfill.\r\n\r\nI think that makes more sense than what it currently says (opaque paths are ones where it is _less_ sensible to try and remove `./` components).\r\n\r\nI'm still a little suspicious about how principled what we're doing there is, but perhaps this at least explains the discrepancy.",
